# Quillback

## Lore

The Quillback is a handsome, curious little humanoid hedgehog or porcupine from the Baalgor Wastelands: small and lean, covered in a thick "fur" of quills from light grey to drab brown, with a rodent-like snout and sinewy limbs. Hunted by every larger predator, Quillbacks survive on high intelligence, raw speed and their quills. They are nomads without large families or permanent homes, recognize one another by scent, and celebrate rare reunions with food, dancing and stories - a good story being funny, exciting and touched with a little sadness, for they lose friends often.

Quillbacks are relentless pack rats who value a thing by how it looks rather than what it is made of, and even the most honest will "borrow" things and forget to return them; about 10% are habitual thieves or kleptomaniacs. Those on Rifts Earth arrived by accident or with slavers, and a friendly, inquisitive Quillback will make the best of it and take up adventure and study.

**Alignment:** Mostly Unprincipled (40%) or Anarchist (45%); a few Scrupulous, Miscreant or Aberrant.

**Size:** 4-5 feet (1.2-1.5 m). **Weight:** 75 to 100 pounds (34-45 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 20-30 years in the wild, twice that in a civilized setting.

**Habitat:** Hot, dry climates from rocky deserts, prairies and scrub lands to forests. On Rifts Earth a Quillback would love Mexico and the western and southwestern United States.

## GM Notes

Anything larger than a Quillback is viewed with suspicion or fear until the little guy gets to know it. Humans, Elves, Dwarves and Faeries are accepted and trusted at once until they prove otherwise - a flaw that has gotten more than one Quillback into trouble, especially with Faeries.
